# Test the Boundaries, Not the Middle

Agents handle the happy path well. They miss the edges. When writing tests, always cover:

## Required Edge Cases

| Category | Examples |
|----------|---------|
| Empty / zero | `""`, `[]`, `{}`, `0`, `None` / `null` |
| Boundary values | off-by-one, max int, empty string vs whitespace-only |
| Large data | 10k items, deeply nested objects, long strings |
| Concurrent access | two requests modifying the same record simultaneously |
| Timezone / date | UTC vs local, DST transitions, leap years, Unix epoch 0 |
| Auth boundaries | unauthenticated request, expired token, wrong role |
| Network failures | timeout, 500 response, malformed JSON body |

## Structure

```
describe("feature name") {
  it("happy path")          // agent usually covers this
  it("empty input")         // you must add this
  it("invalid input")       // you must add this
  it("boundary condition")  // you must add this
}
```

## Red Before Green
The test must fail before the implementation exists. If it passes immediately, the test is wrong or already covered elsewhere.
